<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:14:01Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>REPLAY: Spanish Transport Minister gives press conference on train crash</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e2f36c131fe2f943c0cea9e652ef0de6bb4171679c5bcb1e296683150e78d479</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:14:01Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T14:43:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-replay-spanish-transport-minister-gives-press-conference-on-train-crash" /><summary type="html">A high-speed train collision south of Madrid killed 64 people and injured scores more on Wednesday (October 28), with the toll likely to rise, authorities said in one of Europe's deadliest such disasters this century. Spanish Transport Minister Oscar Puente gave some details in a press conference.</summary></entry><entry><title>Spain: Dozens killed after one high-speed train slams into another</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:53045b8c213e2ff2b90d38121f9b38e07cc53d56b6de21714833656b65f2b965</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:14:01Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T14:34:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-spain-dozens-killed-after-one-high-speed-train-slams-into-another" /><summary type="html">Spain suffered its second deadly high-speed train accident this year when one train on Wednesday, October 28, slammed into another that had stopped on the tracks, with the impact shredding cars and killing at least 64 people. The accident comes with memories still fresh of another crash between high-speed trains in southern Spain in January. France 24's correspondent in Madrid Sarah Morris gives us the latest.</summary></entry><entry><title>Spain: At least 64 dead in high-speed train crash</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a4fe2c5a60ea60f38ca7b8dc50de42e9e345c417fb55b7398d53fab3dafde4c3</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:14:01Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T14:33:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-spain-at-least-64-dead-in-high-speed-train-crash" /><summary type="html">In Spain, a high-speed train slammed into the rear of another train that had stopped, derailing two cars and killing at least 64 people on Wednesday, October 28. The central government’s office for Castilla La Mancha confirmed the death toll had risen. It is the second major train accident in Spain this year.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: Melania Trump-brokered local ceasefire holds for second day</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bac78b89f22e0d4481266b670cd03c610244680810f989384cd36d8e88f3dee3</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:14:01Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T12:42:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-ukraine-melania-trump-brokered-local-ceasefire-holds-for-second-day" /><summary type="html">There ​have been ​no breaches of the US-brokered local ceasefire ​around ‌the ⁠Russian-occupied town of Oleshky ‌in southern Ukraine during its first 30 hours, ​Ukraine's human rights ‌ombudsman Dmytro Lubinets said on ‌Wednesday. A ceasefire has ​been agreed until November 1 to ​allow residents of ​the frontline ​town – who had ​been unable to leave amid near-uninhabitable conditions – to evacuate.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: Ceasefire holds for its first 30 hours in occupied Oleshky</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3c93415711300fef8e075b2b44439e415b28567cfff88bccf46bfcdfc3c818a4</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:14:01Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T10:46:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-ukraine-ceasefire-holds-for-its-first-30-hours-in-occupied-oleshky" /><summary type="html">A local ceasefire in the Russian-occupied southern Ukrainian city of Oleshky held through its first day and night, despite continued fighting between Moscow and Kyiv elsewhere. The truce, which began on Tuesday in the devastated city, is expected to remain in place until Sunday. Emerald Maxwell reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Spain: At least 10 dead in crash between 2 high-speed trains</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2c96ce4c015df413178507cf7ce72423be9bd91298801134d97ffab48e769232</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:14:01Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T10:11:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-spain-at-least-10-dead-in-crash-between-2-high-speed-trains" /><summary type="html">At least ten people have died in a crash between two trains in central Spain. The crash occurred Wednesday morning  in the province of Toledo. Rail service is suspended between Madrid, Ciudad Real and Andalusia.
 
France 24's correspondent in Madrid Sarah Morris reports the latest.</summary></entry><entry><title>At least 64 killed in high-speed train collision in central Spain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:98d5c50ce8830f5cf178fee398fe6342f375227e99c78e36de94f67bf739f0fe</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:14:01Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T09:00:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261028-two-high-speed-trains-collide-in-southern-spain-rail-operator-says" /><summary type="html">At least 64 people have been killed on Wednesday after two high-speed trains collided in Spain's central Toledo province, regional authorities confirmed, with high-speed rail services between Madrid and Andalusia suspended. Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez said Spain would observe three days of mourning.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>How student assemblies brought down the Serbian government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5d269d85ef63bd859516867f0b039fec62bd57e0ffbabe3dea2ae9ea3f9f9071</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:14:01Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T18:58:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261027-how-student-assemblies-brought-down-the-serbian-government" /><summary type="html">A list of academics, engineers, artists and activists chosen by Serbia’s student assemblies defeated long-ruling president Aleksandar Vucic's right-wing Serbian Progressive Party Sunday. The shock victory comes after nearly two years of student-led anti-corruption protests – and may serve as a model for other movements hoping to turn street demonstrations into concrete political change.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>France: Lawmakers hold a minute of silence for Pengo Bossio Wangi, victim of racist attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0b8b323d5e33083475aeffaf25be86bad4d32c59f68b287bac83ab00d21b17b3</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:14:01Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T17:08:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-france-lawmakers-hold-a-minute-of-silence-for-pengo-bossio-wangi-victim-of-racist-attack-1" /><summary type="html">French lawmakers held a minute of silence for Pengo Bossio Wangi. The victim of a racist attack died in a shooting last week, while at least five other people were wounded, including a 12-years-old girl. FRANCE 24’s Claire Paccalin reports from the ground.</summary></entry><entry><title>France's Senate takes on the 'rioters pay' bill after protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9f2e960573d96eebfcb80207d581272a3a7d3fa41a8910f3f05e1f84cde33362</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:14:01Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T14:13:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-france-s-senate-takes-on-the-rioters-pay-bill-after-protests--b3c03807dca7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-france-s-senate-takes-on-the-rioters-pay-bill-after-protests" /><summary type="html">If the French Senate passes this bill, rioters will have to pay for the damage caused during the recent unrest across the country. This "casseurs-payeurs" bill comes in the wake of nationwide violence. This draft law now has an explosive add-on aimed at social media. Senators will vote on whether the government can block platforms that are too slow to act on authorities' reports of dangerous content.</summary></entry><entry><title>Localised Russia-Ukraine ceasefire starts in Ukrainian town facing starvation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:64773c18c1a021b9d5e869185d927d8888bbc27eceea26ff2a85407357ad0329</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:14:01Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T12:34:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-localised-russia-ukraine-ceasefire-starts-ukrainian-town-facing-starvation--26b8d037fc17.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-localised-russia-ukraine-ceasefire-starts-ukrainian-town-facing-starvation" /><summary type="html">A localised ceasefire between Ukraine and Russia took effect early Tuesday (October 27) ahead of a humanitarian mission led by US first lady Melania Trump, as missile attacks resumed in Kyiv. FRANCE 24's correspondent in Kyiv, Emmanuelle Chaze, has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ballon d’Or winner Harry Kane delivers emotional acceptance speech</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3988525fd9f978e8cd5bd8c6f919004ffbe1fa88e0c5f2af8307e07844b1fc4c</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:14:01Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T12:20:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ballon-d-or-winner-harry-kane-delivers-emotional-acceptance-speech--113fa0f87132.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ballon-d-or-winner-harry-kane-delivers-emotional-acceptance-speech" /><summary type="html">Harry Kane became the first Englishman in 25 years to win the Ballon d’Or on Monday. Kane scored 73 goals for club and country last campaign and smashed scoring records at the World Cup, where he captained England to a third-place finish.</summary></entry><entry><title>French protests: Student union leaders vow to keep mobilising</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b5dafbc61db877f99a992f47d929f2a40078f205dcce7f7b035061e08a9b14c3</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:14:01Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T11:18:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-french-protests-student-union-leaders-vow-to-keep-mobilising--5057a3ae5412.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-french-protests-student-union-leaders-vow-to-keep-mobilising" /><summary type="html">In France, after weeks of student unrest, the government announced new school measures. Student union leaders said it's a first step but vowed to keep mobilising as they expected further proposals.</summary></entry><entry><title>'They should be afraid': Serbia's student-led victory over Vučić sends warning to 'corrupt' leaders</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:66759c6a79cb8567433bd7b35a1732218f08d51ab03da00aa553fd0af36b050c</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:14:01Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T08:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261027-they-should-be-afraid-serbia-s-student-led-victory-over-vu_i_-sends-warning-to-corrupt-lead--76d7a665d19f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261027-they-should-be-afraid-serbia-s-student-led-victory-over-vu%C4%8Di%C4%87-sends-warning-to-corrupt-leaders" /><summary type="html">François Picard welcomes Helena Ivanov, associate research fellow at the Henry Jackson Society, a London-based foreign policy and national security think tank advocating liberal democracy, strong transatlantic alliances, robust Western defence capabilities and the international promotion of democratic institutions. Ivanov describes the election result in Serbia as a historic turning point in the country's politics.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>US-EU trade truce at risk over $3.4 billion Airbus loan, Trump official warns</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:18f4afe0eba5cea4524546feef7daaac02808087394952b3d9a77ac59f065978</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:14:01Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T02:20:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261027-us-eu-trade-truce-airbus-loan-trump--677a525d064d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261027-us-eu-trade-truce-airbus-loan-trump" /><summary type="html">US Trade Representative Jamieson Greer warned on Monday that a $3.4 billion European Investment Bank loan to Airbus could jeopardise a tariff truce between Washington and Brussels. Greer said his office had received no details about the financing, announced in June, and urged the EU to resolve the matter quickly.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Europe's top NATO powers pledge greater defence role, reaffirm US alliance</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5e208ec397fa74c852e9992e09db387d0f07ec7867949857987551e2aa070057</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:14:01Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T23:33:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261026-europe-nato-defence-responsibility-us-alliance--7fa969338f30.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261026-europe-nato-defence-responsibility-us-alliance" /><summary type="html">Europe's five main NATO members said on Monday they were ready to take greater responsibility for the continent's security while reaffirming the United States as an "indispensable ally". Defence ministers from France, Germany, Italy, Poland and Britain pledged closer co-operation with Washington after talks in Paris on strengthening Europe's defence role.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Protests in Europe: Fact-checking viral videos amid claims of 'chaos'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a72b2f55ebfbb494644b96bc6f119fc18c2fc01bb6321d69bedb08ac85decc8e</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:14:01Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T22:18:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261026-protests-in-europe-fact-checking-viral-videos-amid-claims-of-chaos--15058a7a9f55.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261026-protests-in-europe-fact-checking-viral-videos-amid-claims-of-chaos" /><summary type="html">As young people protest poor school conditions and the rising cost of living across Europe, misleading videos are spreading online. Footage from Poland in 2017, military preparations in Portugal and a protest in Argentina have all been falsely presented as recent demonstrations in Europe, painting a misleading picture of unrest. Vedika Bahl fact-checks three viral videos to uncover what they really show and how old footage is being recycled to spread misinformation and attract clicks.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>Serbia’s elections: 'Tracking fraud for sure had an impact on the results'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cf50b78f9177c34e3f58112da119bf7aad409fa5a7118f666fbb57971c095c3e</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:14:01Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T21:49:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261026-serbia-elections-tracking-fraud-had-an-impact-on-results-vote-fraud--fc816450d254.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261026-serbia-elections-tracking-fraud-had-an-impact-on-results-vote-fraud" /><summary type="html">On October 25, Serbia's student-led protest movement won a historic victory in parliamentary ⁠elections, defeating outgoing President Aleksandar Vucic's party. Supporters of the student list explained to FRANCE 24 how they mounted a massive mobilisation to fight electoral fraud and monitor the electoral process inside and outside the polling stations.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Serbian student movement eyes power after election triumph</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:05643ba4f529013ae5a40dab56cca2f5cede033eb3f72455c0baf09fbdeebde9</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:14:01Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T19:48:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/serbian-student-movement-eyes-power-after-election-triumph--396143e74db4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/serbian-student-movement-eyes-power-after-election-triumph" /><summary type="html">Emotions ran high in Belgrade on Monday after a student-led movement upset the right-wing populist Aleksandar Vucic's party in Serbia's snap election. A celebratory mood gripped the capital, with drivers honking their horns and passers-by holding up three fingers -- the winning list's ballot number and a Serbian greeting. Many wore badges and other symbols of the student movement, while a large group of residents spent the day cleaning up a park between parliament and the presidency after Vucic loyalists, who had camped there for more than a year, fled. FRANCE 24's Mark Owen speaks with researchers and political activist Aleksandar Matković.</summary></entry><entry><title>French student union leaders call for 'continued mobilisation' after meeting PM</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fe3f0d07f0e3d2f4bb941f1395b1a1f08e04a61e3628a2a47d9c376f5c14d23e</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:14:01Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T17:37:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-french-student-union-leaders-call-for-continued-mobilisation-after-meeting-pm--c60adecb5ed9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-french-student-union-leaders-call-for-continued-mobilisation-after-meeting-pm" /><summary type="html">The French government met student representatives on Monday (October 26) following weeks of unrest. Students who had been demanding a meeting for weeks hail progress. Nonetheless they are now calling for fresh demonstrations next Saturday (October 31) to press for further measures. Details by FRANCE 24’s French Politics Editor Marc Perelman.</summary></entry><entry><title>Macron promises 'concrete measures' in response to French students' demands</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a4af45af42138ee42faf968f2e5232a0fbe8892154802ae72745ee9bce3e5eae</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:14:01Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T14:39:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-french-president-promises-concrete-measures-in-response-to-french-students-demands--507afbcad5c6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-french-president-promises-concrete-measures-in-response-to-french-students-demands" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron said the government would announce “concrete measures" on Monday (October 26) to address school students’ demands after weeks of unrest. Prime Minister Sébastien Lecornu was scheduled to meet with students later Monday. FRANCE 24's Luke Shrago reports from the ground.</summary></entry><entry><title>Serbia's Vucic concedes defeat to the student-led movement: What's next?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ab736e466528236758e67ec02edf74d842da4aa155e6f31636154473a188879a</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:14:01Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T14:12:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/serbia-s-vucic-concedes-defeat-to-the-student-led-movement-what-s-next--ca4d04c9c348.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/serbia-s-vucic-concedes-defeat-to-the-student-led-movement-what-s-next" /><summary type="html">Serbia's student-led protest movement won a historic victory in parliamentary ⁠election, ending the ​long rule of Aleksandar Vucic and sparking mass celebrations. But their yet-to-be named leaders face a long list of issues. FRANCE 24's Angela Diffley gives us her analysis.</summary></entry><entry><title>Belgrade in rapture as Serbian students topple Vucic in historic election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aa6936e2122d7eaaf22f406af18fea1020f75b6f8ee84554340f81173f13eec6</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:14:01Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T13:19:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-belgrade-in-rapture-as-serbian-students-topple-vucic-in-historic-election--2fc33b825db2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-belgrade-in-rapture-as-serbian-students-topple-vucic-in-historic-election" /><summary type="html">Serbia's student-led movement declared victory in parliamentary elections Sunday ending 14 years in power for Aleksandar Vucic's right-wing populist party. Vucic conceded defeat less than two hours after polls closed, triggering raucous scenes in the capital as supporters of the movement celebrated the defeat of a government they blamed for deep-rooted corruption.</summary></entry><entry><title>French PM meets student representatives after weeks of protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7329d68e9efdad09c951243080df0502e21a0d988871a96cd32b6c561ccb33b7</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:14:01Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T12:20:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/french-pm-meets-student-representatives-after-weeks-of-protests--2d535383d1ec.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/french-pm-meets-student-representatives-after-weeks-of-protests" /><summary type="html">French Prime Minister Sebastien Lecornu is set to meet with high school students on Monday afternoon (October 26) to ease tensions in the country after nearly a month of protests. This follows another meeting in which French president Emmanuel Macron promised a concrete response to demands for better education standards and funding.</summary></entry><entry><title>'An everyday habit': 2.5 billion lines of cocaine snorted in England per year</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:41a9c2ac9272302b04a97bec8891e905007a1dc4d105e969d60b7c98212c2bd5</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:14:01Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T11:05:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261026-an-everyday-habit-2-5-billion-lines-of-cocaine-snorted-in-england-per-year--18eafac8cf0a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261026-an-everyday-habit-2-5-billion-lines-of-cocaine-snorted-in-england-per-year" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Monday, October 26: Brazilian and international papers react to Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva's presidential election victory. Next: The New York Times warns that the war in Iran is entering a dangerous new phase. Also: cocaine consumption and cocaine-related crimes are surging across Britain. Finally, it turns out that wrapping children in cotton wool isn't the best parenting strategy.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>'Serbia is free': Belgrade erupts in celebration after Vucic's defeat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c66960e3eab652f1259222a381a68104d2938c1ec586f2b4ed788b530d877664</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:14:01Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T09:55:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/serbia-is-free-belgrade-erupts-in-celebration-after-vucic-s-defeat--a2db51949b5d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/serbia-is-free-belgrade-erupts-in-celebration-after-vucic-s-defeat" /><summary type="html">Celebrations erupted across several Serbian cities late Sunday (October 25) as people hailed the student-backed movement deposing veteran leader Aleksandar Vucic's party in a snap election.</summary></entry><entry><title>Serbia's student movement ousts longtime leader Vucic in parliament poll</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:15900f29a1570e73e38dbcb38b2005209c7e0c035dd32052a439e3e1f55b0d0b</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:14:01Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T09:41:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/serbia-s-student-movement-ousts-longtime-leader-vucic-in-parliament-poll--7c0900459d30.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/serbia-s-student-movement-ousts-longtime-leader-vucic-in-parliament-poll" /><summary type="html">Serbia's Aleksandar Vucic conceded defeat in an historic election on Sunday (October 25) following a near to 70% turnout at polling stations. The snap election followed nearly two years of student-led demonstrations against perceived corruption and authoritarianism triggered by the deaths of 16 people when a train station canopy collapsed in the ‌city of Novi Sad in 2024. FRANCE 24's Laurent Rouy tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Serbia's Vucic concedes defeat in historic snap election with record turnout</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3fae3f724ee47ed5dc080e468344e4698f381c8d7f1d5399d96347bdd23222da</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:14:01Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T21:24:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261025-serbia-s-vucic-concedes-defeat-in-historic-snap-election-with-record-turnout--83a01660e277.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261025-serbia-s-vucic-concedes-defeat-in-historic-snap-election-with-record-turnout" /><summary type="html">Serbia's Aleksandar Vucic conceded defeat in an historic election on Sunday following a near to 70% turnout at polling stations – the highest since the break-up of Yugoslavia in 1992. The snap election followed nearly two years of student-led demonstrations against perceived corruption and authoritarianism triggered by the deaths of 16 people when a train station canopy collapsed in the ‌city of Novi Sad in 2024.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>The week in pictures: Protests across France, wildfires in Indonesia and Brazilian elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:42d0b81fcafbb2810cd92bc64ec8c154f59785e22e6c8fdb2f66807dca459526</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:14:01Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T12:48:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261025-the-week-in-pictures-protests-across-france-wildfires-in-indonesia-and-brazilian-elections--3fb12d327891.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261025-the-week-in-pictures-protests-across-france-wildfires-in-indonesia-and-brazilian-elections" /><summary type="html">From student protests across France over the weekend and presidential elections in Brazil pitting leftist incumbent Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva against right-wing challenger Flavio Bolsonaro to wildfires in Indonesia, FRANCE 24 looks back at some of the most striking images from the past week.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Serbia holds parliamentary election as populist leader Vucic faces student movement</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0fd08e5fbf3376d2e84fc03904a27d4e0874f7677c8e6017dcf984835542cb3f</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:14:01Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T07:14:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261025-serbia-holds-parliamentary-election-as-populist-leader-vucic-faces-student-movement--d43323a472f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261025-serbia-holds-parliamentary-election-as-populist-leader-vucic-faces-student-movement" /><summary type="html">Serbia votes on Sunday in what is set to be its most contested parliamentary election in more than 14 years, as a student-led movement seeks to oust the party of populist leader Aleksandar Vucic. The vote comes after nearly two years of student-led protests sparked by the 2024 collapse of a canopy that killed 16 people.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry></feed>
